Substantial revision work is needed. (2)
{\textgreater} *** Overall Recommendation: What is your overall recommendation of this paper?
Reject (2)
{\textgreater} *** Reviewer Familiarity: Please assess your familiarity with the subjectmatter of the paper.
Familiar with this area of research (2)
{\textgreater} *** Comments: Please justify here your rating of the paper. What are its strengths and weaknesses? Note that these comments will be sent to the authors.
The problem and motivation of the paper is good. The system architecture (Section II) is well-defined to suit the problem. However, the mathematical model proposed in Section III seems decoupled from the system architecture. There is no detailed description of the data quality control algorithms and their task characteristics. An idealised version of tasks have been considered.
The idea of regular task generation for data quality monitoring is good. However, the capability can probably exist either cloud or edge nodes. It is unrealistic to assume that the data collection device can generate tasks based on fluctuations in the data quality.
The simulation experiment chooses certain parameters like task generation rate, propagation delay, and task processing rate. It is better to link these metrics with one or two real world use cases.
On another note, the contents of the figures is excellent but their presentation is somewhat lacking. Please consider redrawing the figures.

},
