	abstract = {Digital Twins (DTs) integrate models with data gathered from Physical Twin (PT) counterparts, adding value through enablers and services that allow informed decision-making about the reconfiguration of the PT, either autonomously, or by human stakeholders.We consider the potential of DTs for improving the capabilities and performance of autonomous systems through two lenses. First, we outline how different agent architectures can integrate DT models to enhance decisionmaking and reconfiguration. Second, we consider how DT technology can further support self-* properties within autonomous (multi-)agent systems.We identify open challenges that we argue need to be tackled in order to improve the utilisation of DT technology for autonomously reconfiguring systems at runtime.},
