	doi = {10.1007/978-3-031-66719-0_9},
	abstract = {A Digital Twin (DT) has great potential as a tool for monitoring, detecting and reporting anomalies. Such advance warning allows stakeholders to sidestep failures, or to be better prepared to recover from them. This chapter introduces modelbased and data-driven approaches to monitoring in DTs. Model-based monitoring uses definitions of properties (expressed in temporal logics) that describe the desired behaviour of the Physical Twin (PT). Data-driven approaches build monitors from historical data collected from the PT using machine learning models. We discuss how these types of techniques can be used to provide anomaly detection, at either the component or system levels.},
