	abstract = {Digital twins are powerful tools for real-time monitoring and control, and simulation and optimization of cyber-physical systems and processes, (cf. the physical twin). The Architecture, Engineering, Construction and Operation (AECO) domain is highly interested in exploiting digital twins, yet struggles with easily establishing these due to a lack of open, publicly accessible twinning platforms. Yet, with the introduction of the Industry Foundation Classes, an open standard for model and data exchange, and the broad availability of public cloud infrastructures, the provisioning of a twinning platform for the AECO domain for the fully automated generation of digital twins of buildings (cf. the physical twin) is feasible. We report on a novel cloud-based platform for automated instantiation of digital twins. Our results demonstrate both the feasibility and relevance of our proposal to reduce the time and effort to implement and the cost to operate a digital twin atop managed cloud services.},
